{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04YV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-trivial-implications}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:34cd970465d0072128031d4ddd39c45c728463ce91b13916272b25ac52a45f58", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ccb91717dd13e16167effcea0e0fdbe82ff7b77c0ecb58da96dbd195ae017a02", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is separated, then <MATH_0003> is quasi-separated.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0004> is DM, then <MATH_0005> is quasi-DM.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0006> is representable by algebraic spaces, then <MATH_0007> is DM.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:561799f100b33f6714cd64a963ee20b55ce177f83065ebe1768ee3f16267435c", "unit_id": "tag:050E:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04YV", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-proper}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-unramified-quasi-finite}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-properties-diagonal-representable}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:39cde34ac839f124b8eb2fff1efeee410aa175628e89cf958ab4d6d121efcf0d", "source_text": "To see (1) note that a proper morphism of algebraic spaces is quasi-compact\nand quasi-separated, see\nMorphisms of Spaces, Definition <REF_0001>.\nTo see (2) note that an unramified morphism of algebraic spaces is locally\nquasi-finite, see\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0002>.\nFinally (3) follows from Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:afaa72676ad886df032a00e8075456d8fc502c9e78b60f5baffae97f541ec046", "unit_id": "tag:050E:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04YV", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:173ce1f84aa06a53528e50d0050771f4319dfa5cae57c6773d9bd5f390320d7d", "source_text": "All of the separation axioms listed in\nDefinition <REF_0001>\nare stable under base change.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b99fbce89249666fe5b57ae09452170ba53b88e082d3980698e0cf25dd8a4ed2", "unit_id": "tag:050F:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04YV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y}' \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : \\mathcal{Y}' \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}'$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Y}' \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta_{f'}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}' \\times_{\\mathcal{Y}'} \\mathcal{X}' \\to\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-base-change-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{definition-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a39e38b9caf3de0da44ca2bb7edc5c32a7f66ffff43d047aaac4843f0f26133b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:80e2f487279f2e1d3201ed45f738190ed7864140a110ade42e8e355d6c4e64c5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and\n<MATH_0002> be morphisms of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0003>\nbe the base change of <MATH_0004> by <MATH_0005>.\nThen <MATH_0006> is the base change of <MATH_0007> by the morphism\n<MATH_0008>, see\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nBy the results of\nProperties of Stacks,\nSection <REF_0002>\neach of the properties of the diagonal used in\nDefinition <REF_0003>\nis stable under base change. Hence the lemma is true.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be9092dfd42202cb3384a0706dbac68466d78991ddc8ec468431b113dc3f9f8b", "unit_id": "tag:050F:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04YV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$W$", "MATH_0004": "$W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to W$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-check-separated-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87955b6b44be14f27ae02579c55634c9110a1b1232924689b9913f16226d9a28", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:30d4ed6344db92bdd4890c96851900774b99fe330d6757f273a0771355a9baec", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a surjective, flat, and locally of finite\npresentation where <MATH_0003> is an algebraic space. If the base change\n<MATH_0004> has one of the separation properties\nof Definition <REF_0001>\nthen so does <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d85cde75e70fde89b63cfac893a57c2a5d36142c58bdb40282109a5a1ae6f9da", "unit_id": "tag:06TZ:statement"}
